        <item>
            <title>1.3.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:06:48 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>7</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Tide 1.3.0</h2>
<ul>
<li>New editor: files now open in Monaco, the editor inside VS Code. You get multi-cursor editing, find and replace, code folding, bracket matching, line moves and comments, and syntax colors for many more languages. Auto-save, the "changed on disk" banner, Markdown preview and session restore work as before.</li>
<li>Cmd-click on a path in command output now opens the file at the exact line and column.</li>
<li>The editor works fully offline, inside the app.</li>
<li>Full-screen programs such as Claude Code or vim keep the keyboard focus when they start, so you can type right away without clicking the pane.</li>
<li>Editor panes no longer show a pane close button over the Markdown preview toggle; each file tab has its own close button.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
