        <item>
            <title>1.1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 15:24:58 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>4</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Tide 1.1.0</h2>
<ul>
<li>Pin tabs: right-click a tab and choose Pin Tab. Pinned tabs stay at the start of the tab bar, show a pin instead of the close button, and come back pinned after a relaunch.</li>
<li>Closing the last tab no longer quits Tide: the window stays open with a New Tab button (or press Cmd-T).</li>
<li>Clicking anywhere in a pane now puts the keyboard on its input, not only the writing area. Selecting text by dragging still works.</li>
<li>After closing every tab, the next launch starts with one fresh tab instead of bringing back the last one you closed.</li>
<li>New Settings window (Cmd-,): choose a default folder for new tabs, new splits and the tab Tide opens at launch, or keep the current behaviour.</li>
<li>Programs like Claude Code can now copy to your clipboard through the terminal (OSC 52), so the "blocked" notice no longer appears. You can turn this off in Settings; reading the clipboard stays blocked.</li>
<li>Tide now appears in Finder's Open With menu for text, code and folders (it never becomes the default app). Opening a folder starts a new tab there.</li>
<li>New services "New Tide Tab Here" and "New Tide Window Here" in Finder's context menu and the Services menu. If they are missing, turn them on in System Settings > Keyboard > Keyboard Shortcuts > Services.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
